    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The file in this repository contains demo data for the LiFE software package: http://francopestilli.github.io/life/ \r\n\r\nThe data set can be used in combination with the function life_demo.m: http://francopestilli.github.io/life/doc/scripts/life_demo.html \r\n\r\nThe file contains:\r\n\r\n(1) Diffusion imaging data acquired at the Center for Neurobiological Imaging Stanford University. \r\n(2) High-resolution anatomical T1w MRI images of the same brain coregistered to the diffusion data.\r\n(3) Three connectomes generated using the same diffusion data in (1) and the tractogrpahy toolbox MRtrix (http://www.brain.org.au/software/mrtrix/). The three connectomes are created using different tractography algorithms. Two connectomes were generated using constrined-spherical deconvolution (CSD) models and either probabilistic or deterministic tractography. The third connectome was generated using a tensor model and deterministic tractography.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Pestilli, F., Rokem, A., Yeatman, J., Kay, K., Wandell, B. (2014). LiFE Demo Data. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: http://purl.stanford.edu/cs392kv3054",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "displayLabel": "Preferred Citation",
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Pestilli F., Yeatman J.D., Rokem A., Kay K.N., Wandell B.A. 2014. Evaluation and statistical inference for human connectomes. Nature Methods. 11(10):1058-1063. http://dx.doi.org/10.1038/nmeth.3098",
            "type": "citation/reference",
            "identifier": [],
            "displayLabel": "Related Publication",
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
